"update": 1,
"values": ["LOIC (Low Orbit Ion Cannon) is an open-source network stress-testing tool that can send massive amounts of traffic to a target server", "Since you've already found the company website's URL, type it in so we can begin our attack", "Lock it in, so we can find their IP Address", "That's their IP Address", "Type it in", "Now these options below are modification for your attack", "Sets how long LOIC waits for a response from the target before considering the attempt failed", "Lets you choose a specific page to attack instead of the website’s homepage", "The custom message data sent with TCP or UDP packets during the attack.", "Specifies which network port on the target to attack", "Lets you choose between attack types", "Controls how many attack requests LOIC sends simultaneously", "If enabled, LOIC waits for a response before sending the next request, making it slower but more realistic.", "Adjusts the overall speed of the attack by changing the delay between packets.", "Let's start our flooding...", "We acivated it, click next to see our results"]
}
